# Cal.com 2024 — Deck design

Full language, Windhawk catalog, and unification plan: `design/CAL-COM-RULEBOOK.md`.

## Tokens

- Canvas `#f4f4f4` + 28px faint grid. Paper `#f9fafb`. Ink `#141414`. Muted `#6b7280`. Chip `#e5e7eb`.
- Stroke `2px solid #141414`. Inactive pills `2px dashed #141414`.
- Radius: pills `32px`, cards `16–20px`, chips `9999px`.
- Shadow `0 4px 0 0 #141414` (hard offset). No glass, acrylic, mica, or soft drop shadows.
- Type: Inter. UI labels uppercase, semibold, ~11–12px, tracking `0.08em`.
- Active control: ink fill, paper text. Idle: paper fill, ink dashed stroke.

## Do

- Native taskbar is top chrome. Desktop page is wallpaper + widgets only.
- Slide-outs (`calc`, `calendar`, `notes`) live in Alt+Space, not a second HUD.
- Action Bar is Cal paper; only the nested xterm is dark-card.
- Windhawk YAML lives in `design/kimi-handoff/windhawk-cal-*.yaml`. Keep `theme: ""`.

## Don't

- Do not add a SaaS / Aetherfield / second theme switcher.
- Do not use serif display, canary yellow chips, 1px hairlines, or 6–8px rectangles as the system look.
- Do not introduce gradients (except the dark-card inner fade from the Figma source).
- Do not glass the Action Bar. Cal paper for the bar chrome (head, prompt, suggestions, footer); nested xterm may stay dark-card (`#131212`).
